  "summary": "Three November 2026 preprints address training, evaluation, and reparametrization of optical neural network hardware.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is optical neural networks treated as trainable physical systems whose value is judged by computed function rather than hardware alone. One preprint uses coarse-grained weak supervision to train optical representation networks, reporting improved classification accuracy for diffractive optical systems. A second proposes evaluating optical neural network modules against performance-matched digital replacements using an expressivity-based methodology. A third reports coding agents training an optical network from camera measurements alone, reparametrized with interpretable optical elements. What is new across the set is a move toward training from weak or measurement-only signals and toward function-level benchmarking against digital baselines. All three are preprints from November 2026.",
